1
00:00:38,539 --> 00:00:41,959
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

2
00:00:45,546 --> 00:00:47,464
That's my house right there.

3
00:00:47,756 --> 00:00:48,923
It's late. You should go home.

4
00:00:48,924 --> 00:00:50,384
But we're almost there.
Why would you...

5
00:00:50,634 --> 00:00:51,677
I'll walk you to your house.

6
00:00:51,885 --> 00:00:54,053
No need,
thank you for walking me home.

7
00:00:54,054 --> 00:00:56,723
You should go home. Thank you.

8
00:00:58,642 --> 00:01:00,268
It's slippery.

9
00:01:00,269 --> 00:01:01,603
- If you don't watch out...
- Mr. Kang!

10
00:01:23,250 --> 00:01:27,004
I was worried you'd end up hurt
if you weren't careful.

11
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:33,468
If anything...

12
00:01:36,305 --> 00:01:37,681
this seems more dangerous.

13
00:01:43,395 --> 00:01:44,396
I'm sorry.

14
00:01:47,524 --> 00:01:49,609
I should get going.

15
00:01:49,610 --> 00:01:52,029
Take care on your way home. Goodbye.

16
00:02:10,756 --> 00:02:12,799
EPISODE 3

17
00:02:24,269 --> 00:02:25,729
This seems more dangerous.

18
00:02:32,944 --> 00:02:35,113
I did save him from danger...

19
00:02:36,990 --> 00:02:39,326
but did I offend him somehow?

20
00:02:40,661 --> 00:02:42,412
Still, I saved his life.

21
00:02:42,871 --> 00:02:44,414
He was being too cold.

22
00:03:22,494 --> 00:03:23,495
Ms. Nam!

23
00:03:29,042 --> 00:03:31,753
No.

24
00:03:33,714 --> 00:03:34,756
Mr. Kang!

25
00:03:35,382 --> 00:03:38,802
I was worried you'd end up hurt
if you weren't careful.

26
00:03:46,935 --> 00:03:47,978
What's this?

27
00:03:50,147 --> 00:03:51,273
What's wrong with my heart?

28
00:03:53,775 --> 00:03:54,901
Do I have a heart problem?

29
00:03:55,569 --> 00:03:58,780
Mr. Kang, have this and cheer up.

30
00:03:59,990 --> 00:04:00,991
Good luck.

31
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:04,201
Mr. Kang, do you drink coffee now?

32
00:04:04,202 --> 00:04:06,955
I thought you didn't drink coffee.
What's gotten into you?

33
00:04:07,372 --> 00:04:08,623
Coffee...

34
00:04:09,583 --> 00:04:10,584
Right.

35
00:04:11,293 --> 00:04:12,544
It's the coffee.

36
00:04:17,424 --> 00:04:18,425
I shouldn't have had it.

37
00:04:21,678 --> 00:04:23,138
It's just the coffee.

38
00:04:56,963 --> 00:04:59,883
Appello.

39
00:05:01,802 --> 00:05:06,640
The Outstanding Employee
of the Year is...

40
00:05:07,307 --> 00:05:08,350
Gosh, it's nerve-wracking.

41
00:05:10,018 --> 00:05:11,269
The winner is...

42
00:05:15,482 --> 00:05:16,650
Congratulations.

43
00:05:17,359 --> 00:05:20,361
It goes to...

44
00:05:20,362 --> 00:05:21,696
Me?

45
00:05:23,114 --> 00:05:24,241
Me?

46
00:05:24,866 --> 00:05:25,867
Come on.

47
00:05:32,541 --> 00:05:33,583
Kang...

48
00:05:35,418 --> 00:05:36,503
Ha...

49
00:05:37,712 --> 00:05:38,880
Gi!

50
00:05:40,674 --> 00:05:41,675
KANG HA-GI

51
00:05:47,013 --> 00:05:48,765
No way.

52
00:05:55,272 --> 00:05:57,440
FLIGHT TICKET TO NEW YORK

53
00:06:04,072 --> 00:06:05,574
No...

54
00:06:06,449 --> 00:06:07,701
This can't be true.

55
00:06:08,785 --> 00:06:09,870
What...

56
00:06:11,079 --> 00:06:12,247
Wait!

57
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:17,460
Mr. Kang, you're the CEO.
You can't pick yourself.

58
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:22,257
I'm also an employee of Appello.

59
00:06:22,674 --> 00:06:24,259
That's still not fair.

60
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:27,262
You know how hard I worked.

61
00:06:27,429 --> 00:06:28,847
I worked harder.

62
00:06:29,973 --> 00:06:32,142
You shouldn't abuse your power
for personal gain like this.

63
00:06:34,978 --> 00:06:35,979
What did you say?

64
00:06:36,605 --> 00:06:37,647
"Personal gain"?

65
00:06:41,651 --> 00:06:44,029
Ms. Nam, how much do you know?

66
00:06:44,654 --> 00:06:45,739
No, I...

67
00:06:46,239 --> 00:06:48,450
- The thing is...
- Actually, forget it.

68
00:06:49,701 --> 00:06:51,912
As of this moment, you're fired.

69
00:06:53,079 --> 00:06:54,080
What?

70
00:06:54,789 --> 00:06:56,957
I said you're fired.

71
00:06:56,958 --> 00:06:58,792
You're fired.

72
00:06:58,793 --> 00:07:03,548
No!

73
00:07:13,516 --> 00:07:14,643
What was that?

74
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:17,020
A premonition?

75
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:19,814
No, no way.

76
00:07:21,691 --> 00:07:23,735
It was just a meaningless dream.

77
00:07:27,572 --> 00:07:28,657
What on earth?

78
00:07:37,582 --> 00:07:38,667
What's with the weather?

79
00:07:43,755 --> 00:07:45,757
Man, things are flying everywhere.

80
00:07:51,054 --> 00:07:52,222
Our stage!

81
00:07:53,890 --> 00:07:56,183
We've got unexpected heavy rain.

82
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:59,020
Roads are closed,
and the winds are out of control.

83
00:08:00,063 --> 00:08:02,147
The brand CEOs might have
a hard time making it.

84
00:08:02,148 --> 00:08:04,191
Right, we'll probably be
the first to arrive.

85
00:08:04,192 --> 00:08:06,193
How bad is the damage?
Do we have confirmation yet?

86
00:08:06,194 --> 00:08:08,238
I'm afraid we won't know for sure
until we see it in person.

87
00:08:40,770 --> 00:08:41,813
Mr. Kang.

88
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:44,441
Get the security personnel
in place first.

89
00:08:45,233 --> 00:08:47,944
Tie down or clear out any equipment
that might shift or fall.

90
00:08:48,278 --> 00:08:49,279
Yes, sir.

91
00:08:50,321 --> 00:08:51,740
Wait. Mr. Kang.

92
00:09:07,005 --> 00:09:08,923
Who already did all this?

93
00:09:09,716 --> 00:09:10,883
Mr. Kang.

94
00:09:10,884 --> 00:09:13,511
Someone covered everything
with tarps here too.

95
00:09:17,932 --> 00:09:19,684
The CEOs haven't arrived yet,
have they?

96
00:09:19,976 --> 00:09:22,854
Yes, who could've done all this?

97
00:09:27,984 --> 00:09:29,486
Wait. Mr. Kang, isn't that...

98
00:09:34,115 --> 00:09:35,283
Who's that over there?

99
00:09:37,744 --> 00:09:38,828
Mr. Kang.

100
00:09:44,084 --> 00:09:45,168
Hello?

101
00:09:45,502 --> 00:09:46,628
You've arrived?

102
00:09:46,836 --> 00:09:48,546
Wait there for a moment.

103
00:10:14,948 --> 00:10:17,658
Mr. Kang, the employees have arrived.

104
00:10:17,659 --> 00:10:19,369
I'll be right back. Please wait here.

105
00:10:37,428 --> 00:10:38,680
I have to save the clothes at least.

106
00:10:46,855 --> 00:10:47,981
Ms. Nam?

107
00:10:49,649 --> 00:10:52,067
Mr. Kang, you're here.

108
00:10:52,068 --> 00:10:54,695
- What are you doing here alone?
- Oh, the clothes.

109
00:10:54,696 --> 00:10:56,405
They're the vendors' assets.

110
00:10:56,406 --> 00:10:57,907
I'm trying to salvage what I can.

111
00:11:03,037 --> 00:11:04,247
Jeez.

112
00:11:05,582 --> 00:11:07,667
Do you realize
how dangerous it is out here?

113
00:11:08,042 --> 00:11:09,252
Why would you be here alone?

114
00:11:10,378 --> 00:11:12,379
I'm sorry. I was in a rush.

115
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:15,091
Let's wrap this up fast
and get somewhere safe.

116
00:11:15,592 --> 00:11:16,593
Okay.

117
00:11:28,396 --> 00:11:29,480
No!

118
00:11:41,034 --> 00:11:43,036
It's dangerous. Stay away, Ms. Nam.

119
00:11:43,995 --> 00:11:45,245
Let's do this together.

120
00:11:45,246 --> 00:11:46,330
Move over there.

121
00:11:46,331 --> 00:11:48,166
Now that we're holding it together

122
00:11:48,666 --> 00:11:50,210
it's not shaking anymore.

123
00:11:54,881 --> 00:11:57,926
Look, the wind is dying down.

124
00:11:58,301 --> 00:11:59,969
I'm sure the rain will stop soon too.

125
00:12:01,679 --> 00:12:03,139
Let's cheer up just a bit more.

126
00:12:08,645 --> 00:12:09,646
How can you be

127
00:12:10,855 --> 00:12:11,898
smiling at a time like this?

128
00:12:12,106 --> 00:12:13,983
You've got to smile
when things get tough.

129
00:12:14,525 --> 00:12:15,818
Don't you know

130
00:12:16,861 --> 00:12:18,863
smiling actually makes things better?

131
00:12:49,018 --> 00:12:50,979
Mr. Kang, we're here.

132
00:12:51,187 --> 00:12:53,731
Let me put this on you.

133
00:13:02,407 --> 00:13:03,408
Good.

134
00:13:03,950 --> 00:13:04,951
Two, three.

135
00:13:07,662 --> 00:13:09,163
Here. Enjoy.

136
00:13:09,289 --> 00:13:10,665
- Have some bread while you work.
- Okay.

137
00:13:13,001 --> 00:13:14,085
Does this need to go up?

138
00:13:15,169 --> 00:13:17,004
Should we set it up? Two, three.

139
00:13:17,005 --> 00:13:19,090
Press it down. One, two, three.

140
00:13:20,216 --> 00:13:22,135
Don't put yourself in danger
like that again.

141
00:13:22,719 --> 00:13:24,095
Safety comes first.

142
00:13:26,556 --> 00:13:27,598
Yes, sir.

143
00:13:29,892 --> 00:13:31,102
Still, I do...

144
00:13:33,271 --> 00:13:34,314
appreciate your intentions.

145
00:13:35,273 --> 00:13:36,274
Excuse me?

146
00:13:36,816 --> 00:13:38,276
- What did you just say?
- I mean...

147
00:13:40,903 --> 00:13:43,156
Nothing. I'm just saying.

148
00:13:49,329 --> 00:13:50,371
Is everything okay?

149
00:13:51,414 --> 00:13:52,622
It's delicious.

150
00:13:52,623 --> 00:13:56,169
Maybe because it's soaked in tears...
I mean, rainwater.

151
00:13:57,003 --> 00:13:58,338
No, I didn't mean that bread.

152
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:03,426
Never mind.

153
00:14:40,838 --> 00:14:42,089
- Careful.
- Okay.

154
00:14:42,090 --> 00:14:44,092
It's not exactly
that we're canceling.

155
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:45,884
If you could just
give us some time...

156
00:14:45,885 --> 00:14:46,968
No, that's enough.

157
00:14:46,969 --> 00:14:49,054
We'll consider this discussion over.

158
00:14:49,055 --> 00:14:50,807
- But...
- Sir, you can't leave like this.

159
00:14:51,265 --> 00:14:53,518
Sir. Ma'am. Wait.

160
00:14:53,976 --> 00:14:55,728
- We're done.
- Wait.

161
00:14:58,356 --> 00:14:59,524
What's going on?

162
00:14:59,732 --> 00:15:02,110
BRB backed out of the contract.

163
00:15:02,693 --> 00:15:04,195
So did Saucebody, Sweetheart

164
00:15:04,737 --> 00:15:05,780
and 9203 too.

165
00:15:07,615 --> 00:15:09,825
I personally called the CEOs
not to worry.

166
00:15:09,826 --> 00:15:11,868
They somehow heard a rumor

167
00:15:11,869 --> 00:15:13,495
about the Appello fashion show
getting canceled

168
00:15:13,496 --> 00:15:15,039
and came to see for themselves.

169
00:15:15,748 --> 00:15:16,957
Looks like

170
00:15:16,958 --> 00:15:19,085
SE leaked some info.

171
00:15:19,502 --> 00:15:21,003
They're signing with SE instead.

172
00:15:25,383 --> 00:15:28,009
Unless our information is sent to SE
in real time

173
00:15:28,010 --> 00:15:29,719
it's hard to find out.

174
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:32,598
Sir, you don't think the spy is...

175
00:15:38,938 --> 00:15:41,398
Would a spy be out here
since dawn working that hard?

176
00:15:41,399 --> 00:15:44,694
Being here since dawn means
they could get the info faster.

177
00:15:51,617 --> 00:15:54,245
- Gosh. Mr. Young-woo, this.
- Okay.

178
00:15:54,745 --> 00:15:55,830
Here you go.

179
00:15:56,956 --> 00:16:00,001
Clear things up here.
I think it's pretty much done.

180
00:16:00,460 --> 00:16:01,668
I'm going elsewhere.

181
00:16:01,669 --> 00:16:03,087
Finish that up.

182
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:06,173
I can't believe
all this is going to waste.

183
00:16:06,174 --> 00:16:08,759
At least we managed
to salvage these clothes.

184
00:16:09,135 --> 00:16:10,678
Everyone worked so hard
on preparing this.

185
00:16:25,526 --> 00:16:26,611
Sir.

186
00:16:28,154 --> 00:16:29,155
Are you okay?

187
00:16:33,034 --> 00:16:34,367
I heard

188
00:16:34,368 --> 00:16:37,121
you salvaged our clothes
by covering them with tarps.

189
00:16:37,371 --> 00:16:38,706
Thank you so much.

190
00:16:41,334 --> 00:16:45,087
What happens to those clothes now?

191
00:16:47,131 --> 00:16:49,967
They were meant for on-site sales
at the fashion show.

192
00:16:51,302 --> 00:16:52,803
I suppose
they'll just sit in inventory.

193
00:16:59,185 --> 00:17:02,563
It's ending
before I even get started.

194
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:05,733
I haven't given up yet.

195
00:17:09,529 --> 00:17:10,654
Excuse me?

196
00:17:10,655 --> 00:17:12,740
It's not over until it's truly over.

197
00:17:13,199 --> 00:17:15,826
Will you trust me
and follow my lead one last time?

198
00:17:26,003 --> 00:17:30,715
Guys, the moment you've all been
waiting for is finally here.

199
00:17:30,716 --> 00:17:33,093
For today's Morning Greetings...

200
00:17:33,094 --> 00:17:37,430
I actually took a shower this morning
because of this guest.

201
00:17:37,431 --> 00:17:40,685
It's the busiest actor
and fashion director these days.

202
00:17:41,018 --> 00:17:43,813
His name literally means "Two cold."
It's Lee Chan. Welcome.

203
00:17:44,146 --> 00:17:46,356
Two, three. We're destiny.

204
00:17:46,357 --> 00:17:48,942
Hello, I'm Lee Chan from D.N.X.
It's nice to meet you.

205
00:17:48,943 --> 00:17:50,235
DJ AN YOUNG-MI

206
00:17:50,236 --> 00:17:52,488
You're still using that greeting?

207
00:17:52,947 --> 00:17:55,073
You've been using it
since you debuted as an idol, right?

208
00:17:55,074 --> 00:17:58,159
Right. But since no one
calls me that anymore

209
00:17:58,160 --> 00:18:00,495
I keep it alive myself.

210
00:18:00,496 --> 00:18:04,874
Do you ever find yourself
wanting to go back

211
00:18:04,875 --> 00:18:06,501
to your D.N.X days?

212
00:18:06,502 --> 00:18:07,545
Of course.

213
00:18:07,878 --> 00:18:10,964
I know a lot of fans are
still waiting.

214
00:18:10,965 --> 00:18:13,467
How are the other members
doing lately?

215
00:18:16,721 --> 00:18:19,181
They all seem to be doing well
in their own lanes.

216
00:18:20,600 --> 00:18:24,895
We always talk about reuniting
someday for sure.

217
00:18:25,521 --> 00:18:29,442
Really? That's going to be
great news for your fans.

218
00:18:30,610 --> 00:18:33,153
On that note, our first song today

219
00:18:33,154 --> 00:18:38,534
will be Dear My Light
from D.N.X's final album.

220
00:18:39,660 --> 00:18:41,203
- Oh, my.
- Jeez.

221
00:18:41,662 --> 00:18:43,956
Are you out of your mind?
How can you hide something like this?

222
00:18:44,290 --> 00:18:46,166
- Calm down.
- Chan.

223
00:18:46,167 --> 00:18:47,584
You can't do this here!

224
00:18:47,585 --> 00:18:48,918
What is it? Say something.

225
00:18:48,919 --> 00:18:50,795
- Get off me!
- Calm down already.

226
00:18:50,796 --> 00:18:51,839
Come on.

227
00:18:53,215 --> 00:18:55,134
- Hey.
- Get off!

228
00:18:55,468 --> 00:18:57,511
- Hey.
- Don't do this to Roy.

229
00:18:57,887 --> 00:18:59,471
- Stop.
- Move. Get out of my way!

230
00:18:59,472 --> 00:19:01,349
- Don't do this too.
- I said, move!

231
00:19:06,604 --> 00:19:07,730
You're no different.

232
00:19:08,773 --> 00:19:11,150
The two of you ruined
everything we built!

233
00:19:40,137 --> 00:19:41,805
ROY, LEAVE THE GROUP

234
00:19:41,806 --> 00:19:46,227
D.N.X OFFICIALLY ANNOUNCES DISBANDING

235
00:20:03,744 --> 00:20:04,745
Hey.

236
00:20:35,609 --> 00:20:37,027
I'm just getting better at lying.

237
00:20:37,653 --> 00:20:39,530
What was that?

238
00:20:40,448 --> 00:20:42,491
No, nothing.

239
00:20:50,458 --> 00:20:51,792
I CRIED SO MUCH TODAY, BUT I'M FINE

240
00:20:53,586 --> 00:20:55,670
THESE AREN'T TEARS OF SADNESS
BUT SUPPORT FOR YOUR NEW START

241
00:20:55,671 --> 00:20:57,423
I BELIEVE I'LL GET TO SEE YOU
SHINE ON STAGE AGAIN

242
00:21:04,513 --> 00:21:07,475
What? What exactly do you mean, sir?

243
00:21:07,767 --> 00:21:09,143
The Appello fashion show

244
00:21:09,435 --> 00:21:11,060
- will proceed tomorrow as planned.
- What?

245
00:21:11,061 --> 00:21:14,063
We already took a big loss. Are you
suggesting we rebuild the stage?

246
00:21:14,064 --> 00:21:16,108
Yes, we must do it.

247
00:21:16,859 --> 00:21:19,487
If the participating brands suffer,
who'd ever want to partner with us?

248
00:21:20,404 --> 00:21:21,781
If we lose them here...

249
00:21:24,825 --> 00:21:26,786
losing the market to SE will only be

250
00:21:28,537 --> 00:21:29,663
a matter of time.

251
00:21:34,919 --> 00:21:36,879
Is there even a place
we can use right away?

252
00:21:37,797 --> 00:21:38,923
Right here.

253
00:21:40,925 --> 00:21:42,551
- Here?
- Yes.

254
00:21:43,469 --> 00:21:45,846
- We'll do an online show.
- What?

255
00:21:52,019 --> 00:21:53,437
We'll use this space as the runway.

256
00:21:53,813 --> 00:21:55,272
We'll set up four stationary cameras

257
00:21:55,439 --> 00:21:57,190
and focus on the looks
against a white backdrop.

258
00:21:57,191 --> 00:21:59,777
Given how small the space is,
won't it look a bit too plain?

259
00:22:00,027 --> 00:22:01,529
The clothes might actually
stand out more.

260
00:22:02,154 --> 00:22:05,824
Our whole thing was an open-air show
accessible to everyone.

261
00:22:05,825 --> 00:22:06,909
It's such a shame.

262
00:22:07,326 --> 00:22:09,786
It's not just a shame.
It's a huge letdown.

263
00:22:09,787 --> 00:22:11,621
We'll have to redirect the audience
to the livestream.

264
00:22:11,622 --> 00:22:12,997
I know this is far from ideal

265
00:22:12,998 --> 00:22:15,668
but keeping our promise
to the partner brands takes priority.

266
00:22:16,669 --> 00:22:17,795
You're right.

267
00:22:19,046 --> 00:22:20,756
How about projection mapping?

268
00:22:22,258 --> 00:22:23,551
Director Lee?

269
00:22:25,344 --> 00:22:27,929
Every brand in this show has
its own concept, right?

270
00:22:27,930 --> 00:22:30,224
We could visualize their keywords

271
00:22:30,516 --> 00:22:32,350
and shift the space's mood.

272
00:22:32,351 --> 00:22:34,894
The models would be walking
in the same studio

273
00:22:34,895 --> 00:22:37,231
but the background
would constantly feel new.

274
00:22:38,190 --> 00:22:41,526
You mean, use the white walls
as screens for a stage?

275
00:22:41,527 --> 00:22:42,736
Right.

276
00:22:43,070 --> 00:22:46,615
That would bring out
each brand's vibe much better.

277
00:22:54,248 --> 00:22:55,665
Can we prepare that in a day?

278
00:22:55,666 --> 00:22:57,710
I have a few references on hand.

279
00:22:59,003 --> 00:23:00,671
Shall we start
matching the outfits then?

280
00:23:01,046 --> 00:23:03,381
Good. Let's get things prepared
as soon as possible

281
00:23:03,382 --> 00:23:05,217
and run another rehearsal tonight.

282
00:23:06,969 --> 00:23:08,094
Let's get to work right away.

283
00:23:08,095 --> 00:23:10,805
- Yes, sir.
- Clear things out quickly.

284
00:23:10,806 --> 00:23:12,390
We're out of time.
Let's pick up the pace.

285
00:23:12,391 --> 00:23:14,476
Looks like we need
to clear this entire area.

286
00:23:15,519 --> 00:23:17,396
Be careful.

287
00:23:17,688 --> 00:23:18,813
One moment.

288
00:23:18,814 --> 00:23:20,440
Sales and Logistics,
prioritize setting up

289
00:23:20,441 --> 00:23:22,526
- the online show equipment.
- Where are you going? Take these.

290
00:23:26,447 --> 00:23:27,656
This concept is too dark.

291
00:23:28,324 --> 00:23:30,701
Planning and Merchandising,
back up Director Lee.

292
00:23:30,868 --> 00:23:32,619
- A bit...
- Get him

293
00:23:32,620 --> 00:23:35,247
whatever feedback,
info, or items he needs.

294
00:23:36,999 --> 00:23:39,126
Hello, sir. We're doing
an online fashion show...

295
00:23:39,418 --> 00:23:41,170
Marketing, you'll be the busiest.

296
00:23:41,503 --> 00:23:43,296
Announce the transition

297
00:23:43,297 --> 00:23:45,840
across all official Appello socials

298
00:23:45,841 --> 00:23:47,760
and notify the partner brands.

299
00:23:48,552 --> 00:23:50,888
Pull keywords for each brand too.

300
00:23:52,681 --> 00:23:54,724
Ms. Kim, the notice is up
on the website.

301
00:23:54,725 --> 00:23:56,351
- Okay.
- The keyword visual aid is done too.

302
00:23:56,352 --> 00:23:58,686
Ms. Da-reum, run that over
to the studio quickly.

303
00:23:58,687 --> 00:23:59,688
Yes, ma'am.

304
00:24:02,191 --> 00:24:03,317
Here you go.

305
00:24:13,452 --> 00:24:15,745
That's our Director Chan.

306
00:24:15,746 --> 00:24:16,830
I like it.

307
00:24:17,414 --> 00:24:18,749
Add sunglasses to this look.

308
00:24:20,292 --> 00:24:21,502
He's so cool.

309
00:24:25,756 --> 00:24:28,675
I hear you're diving
into the fashion business.

310
00:24:28,676 --> 00:24:30,970
Yes. Going forward,
I plan to incorporate the philosophy

311
00:24:31,261 --> 00:24:33,514
of "Unframe,"
which is to break out of the box.

312
00:24:34,473 --> 00:24:37,309
Stiff and standardized fashion
is boring.

313
00:24:38,727 --> 00:24:42,398
I'd really love
to work with him someday.

314
00:24:42,606 --> 00:24:45,942
Everyone dresses similarly
these days.

315
00:24:45,943 --> 00:24:48,611
Even the standards
for being fashionable are similar.

316
00:24:48,612 --> 00:24:51,490
I want to shatter those standards.

317
00:24:59,331 --> 00:25:01,291
We're actually working together now.

318
00:25:06,171 --> 00:25:07,423
It's crazy.

319
00:25:22,646 --> 00:25:25,982
Gosh. I heard you were out there
since dawn cleaning up the site.

320
00:25:25,983 --> 00:25:27,526
I didn't even think of that.

321
00:25:27,735 --> 00:25:28,777
The CEO is different indeed.

322
00:25:30,279 --> 00:25:31,780
Even our newest employee was there.

323
00:25:33,699 --> 00:25:35,451
- I see.
- Okay.

324
00:25:36,869 --> 00:25:39,204
Was she too busy to call me?

325
00:25:40,456 --> 00:25:41,582
- What?
- What?

326
00:25:42,249 --> 00:25:43,250
Nothing.

327
00:25:43,792 --> 00:25:46,962
Whoever it is, their dedication
to the company is remarkable.

328
00:25:47,671 --> 00:25:50,257
- We'll refer to this.
- Okay.

329
00:25:50,466 --> 00:25:51,508
- Thank you.
- No problem.

330
00:25:52,217 --> 00:25:54,094
I think so.

331
00:25:57,181 --> 00:25:58,599
Anyway, tomorrow is the problem.

332
00:25:58,974 --> 00:26:00,517
I have to head out
for a shoot right now.

333
00:26:01,310 --> 00:26:04,396
I'll take care
of the fashion show somehow.

334
00:26:06,607 --> 00:26:08,274
- Let's work this out.
- Okay.

335
00:26:08,275 --> 00:26:09,860
- See you.
- Bye. Let's be in touch.

336
00:26:15,616 --> 00:26:17,451
Wait, Chan is leaving.

337
00:26:33,926 --> 00:26:36,220
Was I gazing happily at Chan
in this mess?

338
00:26:36,553 --> 00:26:38,597
Jeez, I look like an absolute wreck.

339
00:26:42,768 --> 00:26:44,228
MOM

340
00:26:44,978 --> 00:26:47,064
- Aren't you having lunch?
- Let me step out briefly.

341
00:26:47,481 --> 00:26:49,274
- Goodness.
- Gosh, excuse me.

342
00:26:53,403 --> 00:26:54,738
Taxi.

343
00:26:58,450 --> 00:26:59,493
SE CORPORATION

344
00:27:01,662 --> 00:27:04,748
ONLY YOU, PARK SEO-JIN

345
00:27:06,333 --> 00:27:08,752
Please drive a little faster.
Thank you.

346
00:27:12,131 --> 00:27:13,340
It's Mom.

347
00:27:20,305 --> 00:27:22,057
Jeez, this is crazy.

348
00:27:24,768 --> 00:27:25,894
Mom!

349
00:27:26,979 --> 00:27:28,772
- Mom.
- Da-reum?

350
00:27:29,398 --> 00:27:30,857
What brings you here?

351
00:27:30,858 --> 00:27:34,027
I came to see my daughter, of course.

352
00:27:35,404 --> 00:27:37,739
- Come with me.
- What?

353
00:27:40,242 --> 00:27:43,745
You can't just drop by like this
without giving me a heads-up.

354
00:27:44,663 --> 00:27:46,623
Wait, Da-reum.

355
00:27:48,167 --> 00:27:50,126
Do you go to work dressed like that?

356
00:27:50,127 --> 00:27:51,211
Why?

357
00:27:52,087 --> 00:27:55,965
Jeez, you're frumpy and messy.

358
00:27:55,966 --> 00:27:57,176
Look at yourself.

359
00:27:57,301 --> 00:28:00,053
I don't normally dress this poorly.

360
00:28:01,180 --> 00:28:02,973
Something came up.

361
00:28:03,307 --> 00:28:04,850
Anyway, go now.

362
00:28:05,142 --> 00:28:06,476
You're good
now that you saw me, right?

363
00:28:06,852 --> 00:28:09,896
- Go on and leave.
- What... Wait.

364
00:28:09,897 --> 00:28:10,981
Wait up.

365
00:28:11,607 --> 00:28:12,649
Take this.

366
00:28:14,776 --> 00:28:17,821
You didn't have to bring this.
It's heavy.

367
00:28:18,155 --> 00:28:20,574
It's your favorite jangjorim.

368
00:28:21,450 --> 00:28:22,743
I packed just a little for you.

369
00:28:24,828 --> 00:28:26,413
What about the rice cakes
I sent the other day?

370
00:28:26,788 --> 00:28:28,415
Did you share them
with your coworkers?

371
00:28:28,790 --> 00:28:29,875
What did they say?

372
00:28:30,626 --> 00:28:32,669
Well, they...

373
00:28:33,003 --> 00:28:34,046
They loved them.

374
00:28:34,379 --> 00:28:36,589
Right?

375
00:28:36,590 --> 00:28:41,220
I lined up at a famous rice cake shop
from 5 a.m. just to order those.

376
00:28:44,806 --> 00:28:46,225
Mom, I...

377
00:28:47,142 --> 00:28:49,937
The truth is, SE Corporation...

378
00:29:05,869 --> 00:29:08,413
What is it?
Has work been tough lately?

379
00:29:11,541 --> 00:29:12,834
That's not it.

380
00:29:16,338 --> 00:29:18,340
That's how corporate life is.

381
00:29:19,591 --> 00:29:20,676
It's hard on everyone.

382
00:29:23,345 --> 00:29:26,306
But you know
I'm always rooting for you, right?

383
00:29:31,395 --> 00:29:32,479
Mom.

384
00:29:33,313 --> 00:29:34,314
I'm sorry.

385
00:29:36,483 --> 00:29:37,776
Oh, hush now.

386
00:29:38,235 --> 00:29:39,652
I should get going.

387
00:29:39,653 --> 00:29:41,071
It's almost time for my bus.

388
00:29:41,989 --> 00:29:43,699
Let me walk with you.
I'll catch you a cab.

389
00:29:44,658 --> 00:29:47,952
I met the CEO of BRB.

390
00:29:47,953 --> 00:29:50,914
He already signed with SE.

391
00:29:51,873 --> 00:29:54,125
Darn SE.

392
00:29:54,126 --> 00:29:56,920
I wish this building
would just collapse.

393
00:30:10,851 --> 00:30:14,186
- What's wrong?
- Hold on. Let me send you something.

394
00:30:14,187 --> 00:30:15,314
I'm hanging up.

395
00:30:18,358 --> 00:30:19,735
- Thank you.
- What...

396
00:30:21,028 --> 00:30:22,528
You work at SE, right?

397
00:30:22,529 --> 00:30:24,905
I'm running late for an appointment.
Take this.

398
00:30:24,906 --> 00:30:25,949
Here.

399
00:30:27,993 --> 00:30:29,994
- What...
- Wait a second.

400
00:30:29,995 --> 00:30:31,496
Is that how you dress at work?

401
00:30:31,913 --> 00:30:33,331
What do you do with your paycheck?

402
00:30:33,332 --> 00:30:35,500
Dress up a little, okay?

403
00:30:36,752 --> 00:30:38,044
What the...

404
00:30:38,045 --> 00:30:39,379
Let's go.

405
00:30:40,130 --> 00:30:41,590
But that's my taxi.

406
00:30:49,473 --> 00:30:50,766
This is outrageous.

407
00:30:55,395 --> 00:30:57,021
COCOTALK

408
00:30:57,022 --> 00:30:59,149
TEAM MANAGER CHOI SEONG-WOOK

409
00:31:01,693 --> 00:31:02,944
This is Ms. Nam Da-reum, right?

410
00:31:03,445 --> 00:31:05,447
She's not secretly meeting
Director Kim of SE, is she?

411
00:31:32,474 --> 00:31:33,808
Where's Ms. Nam?

412
00:31:33,809 --> 00:31:36,269
She stepped out saying,
"Let me step out briefly."

413
00:31:50,492 --> 00:31:52,701
- Ms. Nam.
- Yes?

414
00:31:52,702 --> 00:31:53,912
Where have you been?

415
00:31:54,663 --> 00:31:57,498
I had urgent business

416
00:31:57,499 --> 00:31:59,375
so I stepped out briefly
during lunch.

417
00:31:59,376 --> 00:32:00,502
What kind of business?

418
00:32:01,336 --> 00:32:04,423
Well...

419
00:32:08,135 --> 00:32:09,344
Well...

420
00:32:09,511 --> 00:32:11,847
A friend wanted to see me real quick.

421
00:32:13,098 --> 00:32:15,724
I don't know what you've been
going around getting

422
00:32:15,725 --> 00:32:17,601
but it's a basic rule
to report when leaving the office

423
00:32:17,602 --> 00:32:19,854
even during a lunch break.
Don't you know that?

424
00:32:19,855 --> 00:32:21,064
Is the company a joke to you?

425
00:32:25,444 --> 00:32:26,736
I apologize.

426
00:32:31,825 --> 00:32:33,576
Listen up, new hires.

427
00:32:33,577 --> 00:32:34,786
Stop assisting for the fashion show

428
00:32:35,245 --> 00:32:37,371
and go back to your regular duties.

429
00:32:37,372 --> 00:32:38,914
We've got things under control now.

430
00:32:38,915 --> 00:32:40,542
And the office needs a skeleton crew.

431
00:32:43,211 --> 00:32:44,463
Mr. Kang.

432
00:32:46,131 --> 00:32:49,134
Can't I help with the show
until the end?

433
00:32:49,718 --> 00:32:51,553
I've been on this
since the rehearsals.

434
00:32:51,803 --> 00:32:54,055
I want to see it through.

435
00:32:57,434 --> 00:32:58,435
Ms. Nam.

436
00:32:59,978 --> 00:33:01,396
Didn't you hear me?

437
00:33:04,483 --> 00:33:05,650
Stay out of it.

438
00:33:23,168 --> 00:33:25,253
Mr. Kang is too harsh.

439
00:33:26,630 --> 00:33:30,926
I mean, you cared enough to rush out
to the site at the crack of dawn.

440
00:33:31,551 --> 00:33:33,345
Are you okay, Ms. Da-reum?

441
00:33:34,638 --> 00:33:36,055
I'm all right.

442
00:33:36,056 --> 00:33:39,600
We're promoting it on socials
and pop-up windows

443
00:33:39,601 --> 00:33:40,727
but how many will actually see it?

444
00:33:41,144 --> 00:33:42,395
Exactly.

445
00:33:42,812 --> 00:33:44,897
Don't you get the feeling

446
00:33:44,898 --> 00:33:48,692
that the online fashion show
is going to flop quietly?

447
00:33:48,693 --> 00:33:49,945
What do we do?

448
00:34:01,289 --> 00:34:02,332
Guys.

449
00:34:04,042 --> 00:34:05,377
Why don't we try doing something?

450
00:34:15,720 --> 00:34:16,721
- Oh, wow.
- Oh, wow.

451
00:34:20,225 --> 00:34:22,059
Ms. Da-reum, you're good at it.

452
00:34:22,060 --> 00:34:24,562
Why do you care so much
about this show, Ms. Da-reum?

453
00:34:24,563 --> 00:34:27,816
Seeing everyone work so hard on-site
made me promise myself

454
00:34:28,900 --> 00:34:32,445
that I'd do my absolute best
to ensure this show's success.

455
00:34:33,697 --> 00:34:35,031
You're so cool.

456
00:34:35,657 --> 00:34:37,033
You can do it, Ms. Da-reum.

457
00:34:41,663 --> 00:34:47,418
Time to put all my fangirl skills
to good use!

458
00:34:47,419 --> 00:34:49,045
Could you make a few adjustments
to the model?

459
00:34:50,505 --> 00:34:52,673
The lighting's too bright
with too much glare on the clothes.

460
00:34:52,674 --> 00:34:53,925
Please adjust that as well.

461
00:34:54,217 --> 00:34:55,260
Will do.

462
00:34:55,885 --> 00:34:56,928
Mr. Kang.

463
00:34:58,388 --> 00:34:59,431
Take a look at this.

464
00:35:02,017 --> 00:35:03,225
We went from this...

465
00:35:03,226 --> 00:35:04,852
OUR FASHION SHOW IS ON AS PLANNED

466
00:35:04,853 --> 00:35:06,354
...to this.

467
00:35:07,522 --> 00:35:08,647
APPELLO IN NAMSAN

468
00:35:08,648 --> 00:35:10,983
OUR

469
00:35:10,984 --> 00:35:13,069
FASHION SHOW

470
00:35:13,278 --> 00:35:15,280
IS ON

471
00:35:15,780 --> 00:35:16,948
AS PLANNED

472
00:35:20,869 --> 00:35:22,579
TRADITION NEVER DIES

473
00:35:24,497 --> 00:35:26,041
THOSE DAYS, THAT FEEL

474
00:35:26,499 --> 00:35:29,169
WEAR CLOTHES OF TOMORROW

475
00:35:31,671 --> 00:35:32,922
NOVEMBER 13, 6:00 P.M., LIVE

476
00:35:33,381 --> 00:35:34,632
What is this?

477
00:35:34,633 --> 00:35:37,469
The rookies made it
to promote the online show.

478
00:35:37,844 --> 00:35:39,053
Isn't it fun?

479
00:35:39,054 --> 00:35:41,890
How about we post it
on our official account?

480
00:35:42,223 --> 00:35:43,224
It's fun.

481
00:35:43,808 --> 00:35:44,809
Whose idea was this?

482
00:35:45,393 --> 00:35:46,436
Nam Da-reum's.

483
00:35:48,605 --> 00:35:50,023
It was Ms. Nam's?

484
00:35:50,482 --> 00:35:51,483
Yes.

485
00:35:52,942 --> 00:35:53,943
Ms. Kim.

486
00:35:54,527 --> 00:35:57,988
Did Ms. Da-reum
handle any sensitive info

487
00:35:57,989 --> 00:35:59,282
regarding the fashion show?

488
00:35:59,824 --> 00:36:01,158
No.

489
00:36:01,159 --> 00:36:04,079
We don't put a rookie in charge
of anything too important.

490
00:36:04,913 --> 00:36:06,623
Why? Is there a problem?

491
00:36:09,000 --> 00:36:10,001
Come with me.

492
00:36:15,882 --> 00:36:17,676
There's something I didn't tell you.

493
00:36:18,009 --> 00:36:19,052
Yes?

494
00:36:25,308 --> 00:36:26,393
Ms. Da-reum.

495
00:36:28,645 --> 00:36:30,397
She worked at SE Corporation.

496
00:36:32,440 --> 00:36:33,525
Yes, I know that.

497
00:36:34,943 --> 00:36:36,985
- You knew that?
- Yes.

498
00:36:36,986 --> 00:36:39,196
She told me she used to work there.

499
00:36:39,197 --> 00:36:40,740
It wasn't on her resume.

500
00:36:41,658 --> 00:36:44,994
She was there for under two months
and thought it would look bad.

501
00:36:45,704 --> 00:36:47,079
She couldn't stand the place

502
00:36:47,080 --> 00:36:49,916
and waited for us
to post about a vacancy.

503
00:36:51,209 --> 00:36:53,128
She didn't even tell her family yet.

504
00:36:53,294 --> 00:36:56,673
Her mom went to SE Corporation
to bring her a lunch box today.

505
00:36:59,843 --> 00:37:00,844
Where are you coming from?

506
00:37:22,490 --> 00:37:25,993
Mr. Kang reviewed the clip you made.

507
00:37:25,994 --> 00:37:27,912
Regarding uploading it
to our official account...

508
00:37:33,418 --> 00:37:35,128
it's a go!

509
00:37:38,590 --> 00:37:41,885
He told me to tell you
you did so well.

510
00:37:42,969 --> 00:37:46,931
Plus, you can all help out
with tomorrow's fashion show.

511
00:37:48,141 --> 00:37:49,434
Can we really?

512
00:37:50,810 --> 00:37:54,647
Post that video on our account,
then go home.

513
00:37:55,190 --> 00:37:56,940
- Okay!
- Thank you.

514
00:37:56,941 --> 00:37:58,358
You did so well.

515
00:37:58,359 --> 00:37:59,651
- Thank you!
- Thank you.

516
00:37:59,652 --> 00:38:00,695
Bye.

517
00:38:09,704 --> 00:38:10,747
Come on.

518
00:38:11,122 --> 00:38:12,207
Let's go upstairs.

519
00:38:18,463 --> 00:38:20,256
- Hyeok.
- Hey.

520
00:38:20,590 --> 00:38:22,008
- You go ahead.
- Okay.

521
00:38:22,634 --> 00:38:23,676
It's been so long.

522
00:38:24,636 --> 00:38:26,429
- Do you have a shoot?
- Sorry?

523
00:38:27,055 --> 00:38:29,015
I was invited on a variety show.

524
00:38:29,390 --> 00:38:31,643
- To do what?
- A bit of this and that.

525
00:38:32,227 --> 00:38:33,228
That's great.

526
00:38:36,689 --> 00:38:39,275
- I owe it to you.
- I didn't do anything.

527
00:38:41,361 --> 00:38:43,821
If you mention D.N.X on the radio

528
00:38:43,822 --> 00:38:46,449
I get to go on TV and reminisce.

529
00:38:49,077 --> 00:38:50,119
Thanks a lot.

530
00:38:58,670 --> 00:39:01,548
"We want
to get back together one day."

531
00:39:04,133 --> 00:39:05,301
Are you serious?

532
00:39:07,720 --> 00:39:08,763
I guess

533
00:39:09,514 --> 00:39:11,641
it takes a lot to be an actor.

534
